<title>GERMANY: Strabag - does not plan to pay 96 dividend.</title>
<headline>Strabag - does not plan to pay 96 dividend.</headline>
<dateline>COLOGNE, Germany 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>German construction group Strabag said on Wednesday that it did not plan to pay a dividend on earnings for 1996, but would instead carry forward its book earnings into 1997.</p>
<p>Strabag said it would carry forward 1.75 billion marks in book earnings and earnings which would be distributed to reserves into the current year.</p>
<p>Strabag said in a compulsory statement that it achieved break-even in 1996.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
